/**
 * Self-contained panel chrome for a standalone (non-facade) `Editor`.
 *
 * Reproduces the app's editor panel (`gep`) toolbar and `⋮` tools menu around
 * the component-owned surface, with **no** app shell, dashboard, `refs`, or
 * Bootstrap required:
 *
 * - toolbar — the Simple Editor switch, Undo, Redo, Clear all text, Copy all
 *   text, and the tools trigger;
 * - tools menu — Format and Keyboard (the latter only when an attached plugin
 *   contributes one), the clipboard group (Select All / Cut / Copy / Paste),
 *   the document group (Toggle Word Wrap, invisible-character highlight,
 *   auto-suggest), and the spellcheck group (the master Spell Check toggle,
 *   one enable/disable entry per available language, the language's own
 *   segmentation command,
 *   and Custom Dictionary);
 * - a Custom Dictionary dialog for the excluded / extra word lists.
 *
 * Only ever built when the component mounts its own surface — the wrap-phase
 * facade (`attachSharedSurface`) keeps deferring its chrome to the application.
 *
 * The heavy lifting is the real app machinery, not a parallel copy: preferences
 * go through `EditorPreferencesStore` (so a standalone editor and the app pages
 * share word-wrap / spellcheck / custom-dictionary settings), and spellchecking
 * runs the real workers via `scripts/spellcheck.ts`.
 *
 * Shared-state note: that spellcheck engine still resolves its target through
 * the page-global `state.editor` (de-globalizing `shared.ts` is a later phase),
 * so while this chrome is attached it points that global at its own Monaco
 * instance and restores the previous value on teardown. Consequence: with more
 * than one standalone editor on a page, spellcheck follows the most recently
 * focused one.
 */

